{
  "body" : "CONTENT BRIEF\nDraw {{subject}} in {{setting}}. Keep the scene sparse and readable, with no lettering or added copy. Add a small handwritten artist signature: \"{{signature}}\". Additional content constraints: {{extra}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\nUse the visual anchors of thin indigo-blue pen contours, loosely doubled and slightly misregistered sketch lines, pale warm-gray paper, and faint cool-gray horizontal notebook rules with a muted pink-red margin line. Render as a simple hand-drawn notebook doodle: {{line_variation}} define the silhouette, with a few lighter construction traces and small uneven overlaps. Keep the drawing mostly unfilled; use the paper as the interior color, with restrained blue line accents and no polished shading. Maintain fine, slightly wavering line weight, crisp but imperfect edges, and a quiet low-contrast page surface. The horizontal rules pass behind the drawing and remain visible in open areas.\n\nDESIGN RULES\nPortrait page, with the subject as a medium-to-large central line drawing and generous blank paper around it. Keep the silhouette visually dominant, with the main recognizable features separated and readable rather than densely detailed. Place the notebook margin near the left edge and let evenly spaced horizontal rules span the full page behind the subject; adapt subject scale and pose while retaining this simple centered rhythm.\n\nAVOID\nAvoid filled color blocks, vivid saturated palettes, heavy black outlines, smooth vector-perfect contours, dense background scenery, dramatic lighting or cast shadows, glossy rendering, and decorative typography.\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\nVariables: {{subject}}, {{setting}}, {{line_variation}}, {{extra}}",
